{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"biophilic-unsecular-krill","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Outbound CREATE against DC produces no binding: `get_jira_key` returns None after the pass\n\n## Provenance\n\nSurfaced live by harness run **30834117797** (job 91755000385, main @ `25ead49f3e`) by story 5200's\nNEW row-1-outbound cell (`test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers`, landed in change\n1283). Its author flagged the create-and-bind SETUP as the likeliest first failure precisely\nbecause no prior live cell exercises an outbound CREATE against DC — every other outbound cell\nmutates an issue that already exists and is already bound. The prediction was correct.\n\n## Evidence — verbatim from the run\n\n> the outbound pass did not create-and-bind '654e-8c11-d632-4a01' (get_jira_key returned None), so\n> there is no DC issue to read the provenance markers off. Row 1's markers are written INSIDE the\n> create (`dispatch_one.py:306-307`), so a missing binding is upstream of this oracle, not a marker\n> finding.\n\nThe cell localises the failure itself: this is **not** a provenance-marker defect. The pass did not\nproduce a bound DC issue for the local ticket at all, so the oracle never got as far as reading\nmarkers.\n\n## Why this is filed rather than folded into 5200\n\n5200's remaining work was \"run the harness and read the verdicts\"; this is a product finding the\nrun produced, and burying an unexplained outbound-create failure in a story's comment thread is how\na defect of this class survives. It is also the SIXTH instance of the epic's recurring shape —\n\"Cloud has the translation, DC never got its half\", every instance a SILENT success where the pass\nreports OK.\n\n## What is NOT yet established, stated plainly\n\nWhether the create was never PLANNED (the differ emitted nothing for an unbound local ticket),\nwas planned but not DISPATCHED, or was dispatched and the binding write failed. Those are three\ndifferent defects. The harness output does not separate them, and `dispatch_one.py:571-578`-style\nwarn-and-continue swallowing means a dispatch failure would look identical to a planning gap from\nthe outside.\n\nNote also that this cell is the ONLY live coverage of an outbound create against DC, so there is no\nprior green run to bisect against — the path may never have worked.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the failing STAGE is identified — planned / dispatched / bound — with the evidence that\n      distinguishes it from the other two\n- [ ] the root cause is proven, not inferred, and recorded here\n- [ ] the fix makes `test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers` GREEN on a live harness\n      run, with the run id recorded\n- [ ] an outbound create that fails to bind surfaces an operator-visible signal rather than a pass\n      that reports OK (consistent with [rebar:39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b] AC4)","id":"18a5-2bd8-3e56-4bd8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Outbound CREATE against DC produces no binding: get_jira_key returns None after the pass"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785779246632229001,"uuid":"8c3fa5d0-92e8-4b3e-b401-657407e1d636"}